# 📱 Google Play Store Machine Learning & Data Analysis

## 🌟 Project Overview
This repository contains an upgraded and professional Google Play Store analysis notebook built for **data exploration, visualization, and predictive modeling** using machine learning.

Leveraging a real dataset of Android applications, this project demonstrates a complete analytical workflow — from data cleaning and feature engineering to model training and evaluation — helping understand key factors that influence app performance and success. :contentReference[oaicite:1]{index=1}

---

## 🎯 Objectives
- Clean, preprocess, and transform raw Play Store data  
- Conduct advanced exploratory data analysis (EDA)  
- Engineer impactful features for machine learning  
- Train, evaluate, and compare multiple ML models  
- Identify patterns and insights that help app developers and analysts

---

## 📊 Dataset Summary
The Google Play Store dataset contains information about thousands of apps, including:

- App name  
- Category  
- Rating  
- Reviews  
- Size  
- Installs  
- Type (Free/Paid)  
- Price  
- Content Rating  
- Genres  
- Last Updated  
- Android Version :contentReference[oaicite:2]{index=2}

This dataset reflects user preferences and app characteristics across the Android ecosystem, making it excellent for machine learning tasks and business insights.

